<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # My Evening Routine – Lesson # 4</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 4</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Writing</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 3rd Grade (CEFR: A1.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> My Evening Routine</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> First, I Brush My Teeth.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Writing: Productive: Create descriptive captions for images with simple words. Interactive: Edit a co-constructed text.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Writing: Can create captions for images of bedtime routines (e.g., "Time to sleep."). Can edit and improve a co-constructed text about bedtime routines (e.g., revising "I brush my teeth." to "First, I brush my teeth. Then, I put on my pajamas. Last, I go to bed."). Can write short phrases and sentences on bedtime routines collaboratively (e.g., "I am sleepy.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays flashcards of various evening routine actions (e.g., 'brush teeth', 'put on pajamas', 'read a book', 'go to bed'). Students call out the actions. The teacher writes the key verbs and nouns on the board as students say them (e.g., brush, teeth, pajamas, book, bed).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models writing a simple sentence for one of the flashcards, e.g., pointing to 'brush teeth' flashcard and saying, "First, I brush my teeth." while writing it clearly on the board. The teacher highlights the word "First" and "brush my teeth" (pronouncing /b/ in 'brush' and /t/ in 'teeth' distinctly). Then, the teacher models blending /t-iː-θ/ in "teeth" and /w-ɒ-ʃ/ in "wash" (if applicable from previous lessons as a warm-up reminder) for reinforcement.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What do I do first?" (Pointing to 'brush teeth' sentence). Expected answer: "Brush your teeth."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Is this about morning or night?" Expected answer: "Night."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[5-7 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "My Evening Routine")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A simple illustrated story or sequence of 4-5 pictures showing a child's evening routine, each with a single, clear caption (e.g., "First, I wash my face.", "Then, I put on my pajamas.", "Next, I read a book.", "Last, I go to bed."). The material is a narrative excerpt focusing on sequential actions for 3rd Grade students.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Identifying and describing sequential actions in an evening routine using simple written phrases.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist question:</b> The teacher asks, "What is the story about?" Students respond: "Evening routine." or "Before bed."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False:</b> The teacher reads sentences about the story, and students signal True or False. E.g., "The child brushes teeth first." (True/False). "The child eats breakfast last." (True/False).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Information matching:</b> The teacher points to a picture and asks, "What word tells us what happens first?" (Students identify "First"). Or, "What verb is in this sentence?" (e.g., "wash", "read", "sleep").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[8-10 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Writing)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students will practice writing sentences using sequencing words (First, Then, Next, Last) and present simple for daily routines, incorporating vocabulary like 'brush', 'teeth', 'pajamas', 'bed', 'sleepy', 'book'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. Sentence Completion (Controlled Practice):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with images of evening routine steps (e.g., brushing teeth, putting on pajamas). Below each image, there is a sentence with a blank. Students complete the sentences using sequencing words and target vocabulary. Example: "_____, I brush my ______." "Then, I put on my _______."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Jumbled Sentences (Semi-controlled):</b> The teacher writes 3-4 simple sentences about an evening routine in a jumbled order on the board (e.g., "I go to bed.", "I read a book.", "I put on my pajamas."). Students copy them into their notebooks in the correct sequence, adding "First, Then, Last" as appropriate. The teacher models the first sentence as an example.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>3. Collaborative Caption Writing (Pair Work):</b> In pairs, students receive a set of 3 new, simple images of a child's evening routine (different from presentation, e.g., 'yawning', 'drinking water', 'closing eyes'). For each image, they collaboratively write one simple caption using a provided sentence frame (e.g., "First, I ______.", "Then, I ______.", "I am _______."). Teacher circulates, providing support with vocabulary and spelling, ensuring correct use of present simple verbs and time expressions like "I am sleepy." or "It's bedtime."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[12-15 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "My Evening Routine")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Individual creative writing and collaborative editing.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>1. "My Bedtime Story" Booklet Creation:</b> Each student receives a small, blank booklet (or a folded paper) with 3-4 blank spaces for drawing and writing. Students are instructed to draw their own evening routine steps in sequence. For each drawing, they write a simple caption describing the action, using sequencing words (First, Then, Last) and vocabulary from the lesson (e.g., "First, I wash my face.", "Then, I wear my pajamas.", "Last, I go to bed."). They are encouraged to include an expression like "I am sleepy." or "Goodnight!" in their last caption.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>2. Collaborative Editing:</b> Students exchange their booklets with a partner. Each pair checks their partner's captions for clarity, correct use of sequencing words, and appropriate vocabulary. They can suggest small improvements (e.g., adding "my" before "teeth," or making a sentence more complete). The teacher encourages polite feedback: "Can you make 'I brush teeth' into 'First, I brush my teeth'?" This addresses the sociolinguistic aspect of asking for help politely.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[10-12 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Observation checklist during production and quick review of student booklets.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students submit their "My Bedtime Story" booklets with illustrated captions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of at least two sequencing words (e.g., "First, Then, Last").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Inclusion of at least three target vocabulary words (e.g., 'teeth', 'pajamas', 'bed', 'book').</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of captions (easy to understand based on drawings).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Evidence of collaborative editing (student-made corrections).</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick self-reflection:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I can write about my evening routine using First, Then, Last. (Yes/No/A little)"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"I helped my friend make their writing better. (Yes/No)"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[5-7 min]</td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was easy to write today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What part of writing about my evening routine was difficult?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson? (e.g., collaborative editing, visual prompts for writing).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What adjustments or additional scaffolds are needed for the next lesson, especially for students struggling with sentence structure or vocabulary? (e.g., more sentence frames, review of verbs).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How did the focus on writing captions and editing align with the learning outcomes?</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> The written routines and edited texts will serve as a basis for Lesson 5, where students will share their routines (mediation activity) and consolidate learning into a final project.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">[3-4 min]</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>